# Example environment configuration for the Tari Ootle Liquidity Protocol frontend.
#
# EVERY value here is PUBLIC: Vite embeds VITE_* variables into the shipped
# bundle. Never place a secret in this file or in any VITE_* variable.
# Copy to `apps/web/.env.local` for local development.

# --- network -------------------------------------------------------------
# Allowed: esmeralda (default) | localnet. Anything resembling mainnet is
# refused: the build reports a blocking error instead of starting.
# VITE_TARI_NETWORK=esmeralda

# --- discovery / indexer -------------------------------------------------
# Optional ADDITIONAL discovery origin (https in production builds). The
# verified Esmeralda defaults are built in and are used when this is unset, so
# an ordinary deployment needs no configuration here:
#
#   https://ootle-indexer-a.tari.com
#   https://ootle-indexer-b.tari.com
#
# Those are the current public Esmeralda `tari_indexer` origins, re-read live on
# 2026-10-01 AFTER the testnet reset (0.42.0, network "esmeralda", network_byte
# 38, epoch 11714). The same two hosts served the pre-reset network, so they did
# not change across the reset. Setting this adds an origin; it does not replace
# the defaults. The CSP `connect-src` list is derived from the same table, so an
# origin added here is NOT automatically permitted by CSP and the build will
# still block it �?" add it to `CONNECT_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in
# apps/web/src/lib/deploymentHeaders.ts if you genuinely need a third origin.
# See docs/LIVE_TESTNET_EVIDENCE.md for the captured observations.
# VITE_INDEXER_URL=https://ootle-indexer-a.tari.com

# --- development-only flags ---------------------------------------------
# Both flags are refused by a PRODUCTION build: the bundle shows a blocking
# notice and the feature stays disabled. They cannot be "shipped on".
#
# Fixture market data (development builds only):
# VITE_USE_FIXTURE_DATA=1
#
# Development wallet providers, e.g. a local walletd (development builds only):
# VITE_ENABLE_DEV_PROVIDERS=1
# VITE_WALLETD_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5100/json_rpc

# --- security-sensitive --------------------------------------------------
# Real cross-chain (XTM/TARI) testnet submission is gated OFF by default at the
# coordinator. Setting the NON-VITE variable below in the coordinator's
# environment enables TESTNET real submission; mainnet never passes the gate.
# This is NOT a VITE_ variable: the frontend only mirrors and displays the
# gate's state, it cannot flip it.
# TARI_LIQUIDITY_ENABLE_REAL_CROSSCHAIN_SUBMIT=1
